first apply allignment to largets member of struct
then divide into 8 byte chunks. (so { i8 i32 i8 } becomes { i64, i8 })
floating point values go into SSE registers, so they become <2 x float> for  { f32, f32 }

floats also get aligned to largest member and divided into 8byte chunks
"If the size of an object is larger than four eightbytes, or it contains unaligned fields, it has class MEMORY"
"f the size of the aggregate exceeds two eightbytes and the first eight-byte isn’t SSE or any other eightbyte isn’t SSEUP, the whole argument is passed in memory."
